/-! # Proposition 6.2(i): distinctness of the primes `(B_i)`, pairs (3, 5), (3, 6), (3, 7), (3, 8), (4, 5), (4, 6), (4, 7)

For each pair `i < j` above the same rational prime `p`: an element `x = B_i + c B_j B_m` (`B_m` a unit) with
`p ∤ N_{L₂₄/ℚ}(x)` (`normInt`), via the relative norm to `L₈` (`normL8`) and an LU certificate (`norm`);
hence `(B_i) ≠ (B_j)` (`span_ne`). -/

